    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0938" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500. A 4e/100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation, China Tariff
                        Revision Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Arnold</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1921-09-09T12:45:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1921-09-01T00:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>].<lb/>[Received September 9, 1922—12:45
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Does Department consider completed draft revised tariff as agreed by Shanghai
                    Commission must be submitted for Department’s sanction <pb facs="0939" n="819"
                        xml:id="pg819"/> before final publication by Revision Commission? Is
                    American delegation’s sanction to completed draft sufficient for American
                    Government ratification?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arnold</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
